# Splashy Spellcaster: "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a Sorcerer Role token attached to up to one other target
# creature you control." On turn 1 Bot1's first Opt is cast while the Spellcaster is its only creature: it is not a legal target
# ("other"), so the trigger goes on the stack with no target (up to one) and makes no Role. A creature spell (Ornithopter, a 0/2) does not trigger it. The second Opt
# does: the Spellcaster is refused as a target and the Ornithopter gets a Sorcerer Role (+1/+1, so a 1/3). On turn 2 Bot2's own Ancestral Recall
# does not trigger it, and Bot2 casts an Ornithopter of its own. On turn 3 Preordain (a sorcery) cannot give Bot2's Ornithopter a Role
# ("creature you control") and puts a second Sorcerer Role of the same controller on the Ornithopter, so
# the first goes to the graveyard (CR 704.5z) and it is still a 1/3 with one Role.

